    mut_param_annotation_no_reference_propagation_2026-07-20, 1, "revalidated 2026-11-02 (close-invalid lane): validity=uncertain - cited source file still present and no evidence it stopped reproducing; keep open"
    mut_param_annotation_no_reference_propagation_2026-07-20, 2, "2026-11-04 hirmir-p2-w1 triage: reproduced on the 2026-11-04 seed (bin/simple.exe run prints n = 41). Syntax quick reference states mut T is a proposal and not enforced through bin/simple, so this is a semantics decision (implement by-reference primitives vs fix spec), not a code fix. Deferred pending owner decision."
    mut_param_annotation_no_reference_propagation_2026-07-20, 3, "2026-11-10 status fixing->open: stale sweep claim, no lane active; reopened for P2 burn-down"
    mut_param_annotation_no_reference_propagation_2026-07-20, 4, "2026-11-10 p2-mutparam lane (Fable): premise holds per memory.md Rule 4 (mut T param = exclusive access, writes OK). Root cause (HIR half): `x: mut T` parses to Reference(T,true) and lowers to HirTypeKind.Ref(T,true), but HirParam.is_mutable was taken only from the `mut x: T` name-prefix side table, so MIR function_lowering is_mut_param took the by-value copy path for the type spelling. Fix: class_declaration_lowering.spl lower_param sets is_mutable = p.is_mutable or type is Ref(_, true). Spec test/01_unit/compiler/20.hir/mut_type_param_reference_propagation_spec.spl 3/5 -> 5/5 (siblings: name-prefix, mut struct, plain, &T). REMAINING, kept open: primitive `mut i64` write-through still needs a by-reference calling convention (call-site address-of + callee load/store through MirTypeKind.Ref) in 50.mir and the Rust seed interpreter still binds by value (bin/simple.exe run prints n = 41 for both spellings); parser_type_annotations_spec.spl:255 stays red until then."
    mut_param_annotation_no_reference_propagation_2026-07-20, 5, "2026-11-11 p2-mutparam2 lane (Opus): MIR half done. 50.mir by-reference calling convention for `x: mut <Int|Float|Bool|Char>` (HIR Ref(T,true)): caller passes MIR Ref(Mutable) of the named local (switch_operators_calls.spl arg loop), callee Loads the value on entry and binds the param symbol to it (function_lowering.spl), MirBuilder.set_terminator Stores it back before every Ret (mir_data.spl mut_ref_param_ptrs/values, reset in begin_function). Spec test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/mut_primitive_param_by_reference_spec.spl 4/7 -> 7/7 (controls: plain by-value, mut struct, mut array, early-return store-back). HIR sibling spec 5/5; closure_capture_write_spec 7/19 unchanged (pre-existing). REMAINING, kept open: Rust seed interpreter still binds mut primitives by value (bin/simple.exe run prints n = 41); non-NamedVar args (field/index places) and method-call args are not passed by reference yet; native end-to-end run not verified."

